# Web SEO: pSEO templates

Public programmatic routes render in `+page.svelte` — **no** thin `*Page.svelte` wrappers that only forward props (**web-conventions** §7). Catalog copy and FAQ items come from server load / constants (**web-seo-pseo**).

## Template ↔ route map

| Route pattern | Primary template / components |
| --- | --- |
| `/` | `LandingPage.svelte`, `HeroMain.svelte` |
| `/channels` | `PublicChannelsHubGrid.svelte` + hub `PublicFaq` |
| `/channels/{slug}` | `PublicChannelHero.svelte` or `PublicComingSoonIntegrationPage.svelte`; `HeroWithLeftMedia` / `HeroWithRightMedia` + `BentoPublicChannelFeature`; `PublicFaq` |
| `/agents` | `PublicAgentsHubGrid.svelte` |
| `/agents/{slug}` | `PublicAgentLandingPage.svelte` or `PublicMcpLandingPage.svelte` |
| `/agents/{slug}/{channelSlug}` | Same agent/MCP landing template; channel-specific VM |
| `/tools` | Tools hub cards + hub `PublicFaq` |
| `/tools/humanizer`, `/tools/humanizer/{channelSlug}` | `HumanizeToolPage.svelte` |
| `/tools/photo-editor`, `…/{channelSlug}` | `PhotoEditorToolPage.svelte` |
| `/tools/skill-builder`, `…/{channelSlug}` | `SkillBuilderToolPage.svelte` |
| `/tools/best-time-to-post`, `…/{channelSlug}` | `BestTimeToPostToolPage.svelte` |
| `/compare`, `/compare/{a}/{b}` | Compare hub grid / detail presenter sections + `PublicFaq` |
| `/creators`, `/creators/{userSlug}` | Creators hub / profile templates + hub `PublicFaq` on index |
| `/roadmap` | Roadmap board + hub `PublicFaq` |
| `/alternatives`, `/alternatives/{slug}` | `PublicAlternativesPagePresenter` patterns |
| `/playbooks`, `/building-blocks` | Hub loaders + `Pagination.svelte` (no infinite scroll on indexable grids) |

Shared chrome: `PublicArea.svelte`, `Footer.svelte` (`PUBLIC_FOOTER_LINKS` — **web-seo-pseo**).

## Section order

### Channel / agent channel landings

1. Hero (`PublicChannelHero` or coming-soon hero).
2. Three feature rows (`HeroWithLeftMedia` / `HeroWithRightMedia` — alternate `mediaOnRight`).
3. Audience / who-is-for (agent pages).
4. Listings preview (playbooks + building blocks by tag) when not coming soon.
5. CLI or MCP command reference (agent hosts / MCP clients).
6. **FAQ** — `<PublicFaq>` with VM `faqSubtitle`, `faqTitle`, `faqDescription`, `faqItems`.
7. No extra bottom CTA block — pricing CTA lives in hero and feature rows only (**add-social-provider-integration**).

### Tool pages (humanizer, photo editor, skill builder, best time to post)

1. Breadcrumb / hub link back to `/tools`.
2. Hero + interactive panel (composer, calculator, canvas).
3. Channel hub grid (`*ChannelHubGrid.svelte`) when generic tool route.
4. Docs or accent CTA banners (`AccentSplitCtaBanner`, `CenteredDarkCtaBanner`).
5. **FAQ** — `build*FaqSection(slug, label)` or generic section from constants.
6. Guest auth funnel on mocked workspace UI (**web-public-auth-funnel**) — sample labels, lock badges, sign-up/sign-in dialog.

### Main hub indexes (`/channels`, `/tools`, `/compare`, `/creators`, `/roadmap`)

1. Hero or intro copy from server load.
2. Grid / list of child routes (crawlable `<a href>` links).
3. **FAQ** — import from `public*HubFaqConfig.ts`; pass items to `PublicFaq`.

Category/tag sub-hubs: grid + pagination only — **no** `PublicFaq` unless product adds a dedicated config.

## `landingHeroTheme`

`web/src/lib/ui/templates/landing-page/landingHeroTheme.ts` drives gradient highlights in `HeroMain` and agent/channel heroes.

- Append new product names to `LANDING_HERO_TITLE_HIGHLIGHT_WORDS` when `heroTitle` should emphasize a label (case-insensitive; multi-word phrases need the full string).
- Rotating landing copy: `LANDING_HERO_HOURS_ROTATE_TEXTS`, `LANDING_HERO_SLOGAN_NOT_ROTATE_TEXTS`.

When adding an agent host or MCP client, update highlights in the same PR as the seed (**add-agent**).

## CTAs and pricing funnel

| Surface | CTA pattern |
| --- | --- |
| Channel detail | **One label everywhere:** `Get Started For Free` → `/pricing` (via presenter `secondaryCtaText` / `secondaryCtaHref`) |
| Tool pages | `PUBLIC_BANNER_CTA_TEXT` / sign-up paths from `centeredDarkCtaBannerCopy` and tool-specific banner copy |
| FAQ connect answers | Prefer `publicFaqHref.signUp` and `connectChannelsGuide` over operator docs (**web-seo-pseo**) |

Do not add login-dependent hero CTAs on indexable landings. FAQ and banners may link `/sign-up` and `/pricing` for trial questions.

## JSON-LD in templates

- **Only** `<JsonLdHead schemaData={schemaData} />` — `schemaData` from load (`$derived(data.schemaData)`).
- **No** inline `<script type="application/ld+json">` or object literals in `+page.svelte` (**web-seo-jsonld**).

## FAQ blocks

```svelte
<PublicFaq
  faqSubtitle={faqSubtitle}
  faqTitle={faqTitle}
  faqDescription={faqDescription}
  faqItems={[...faqItems]}
/>
```

- Items: `{ title: string; description: string }` — `description` is HTML from `faqLink` helpers.
- `FaqAccordion` runs `prepareBlogRichTextForDisplay` + `rewriteHtmlHostedMarketingHrefs` before render.
- Hub configs: spread readonly arrays (`[...PUBLIC_CHANNELS_HUB_FAQ.faqItems]`) when passing to `PublicFaq`.

## Guest mocks (tools)

Public tool UIs mock workspace features without OAuth or post APIs:

- `pointer-events-none` on mock shells; lock toolbars clickable (**web-public-auth-funnel**).
- Label samples as preview — not “Connected channels”.
- Channel-specific tool routes preselect the matching mock channel.

## Related rules

- Catalog constants, FAQ funnel, ASD-STE100: **web-seo-pseo**
- SSR meta + canonical: **web-seo-meta-tags**, **web-seo-canonical**
- Landing/pricing CMS FAQ: **web-seo-cms-copy**
